  "notes": [
    "Throughput is the rate at which successful runs completed, from the first completion to the last in each level. Claim latency is queued to leased; end-to-end is created to completed; both come from the run records.",
    "Subsystem counters are summed over every server replica's /metrics and include background work (heartbeats, maintenance, gauges) during the level; per-run values divide by the runs that finished.",
    "The saturation attribution is a heuristic that compares each level with the first; read the evidence column. Worker capacity and the load generator are not part of the control plane: when either saturates first, the control plane's ceiling is above the measured numbers.",
    "This sweep saturated outside the control plane (worker capacity); add slots or shorten runs to push the control plane further.",
    "Servers, workers, every fake harness process, and the load generator share one machine, so host CPU is part of what saturates; HostLoadAverage records the one-minute load average after each level."
  ]
